From 75c6547e616021428203cc3c6f761da2b9b3136c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:17:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec_decode): price MMA tile knees, 64-row wave
 saturation, and context bands in _step_cost

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478ba1fd70aa4b700e7e467c46960c9888fb.

Rationale:
On NVIDIA GB10 (48 SMs, sm_121a) and the tp4-ring 4-boot engine grid, AdaptiveVerificationManager._step_cost() previously applied HIGH_ROW_COST_SCALE = 0.55 to all verification rows above HIGH_ROW_COST_KNEE = 16 with no upper bound and ignored request context length except when global KV pool occupancy exceeded 70%:
1. In the 33..64 row decode_64 band at high concurrency (num_reqs >= 10, e.g. c16), the 3rd and 4th 16-row Tensor Core MMA tiles coalesce across already-active routed MoE experts and the single decode_64 launch at a 0.28x marginal row cost (0.136 ms/row vs 0.492 ms/row base unit on the tp4-ring grid), while lower concurrency (num_reqs < 10, e.g. c8) remains at 0.55x.
2. Above R = 64 rows on 48 SMs, dense projections cross DECODE_ROWS = 64 into prefill_128 and _index_chunk crosses DECODE_CHUNK = 64 into a second 64-row wave, incurring a discrete 3.301 ms step jump (SECOND_WAVE_STEP_ROWS = 6.714 row units on the tp4-ring grid) at SATURATED_ROW_COST_SCALE = 0.28. A single request spilling past 16 rows (copy-draft burst) has no cross-request expert coalescing and pays 1.0x plus SINGLE_REQ_TILE_STEP_ROWS = 1.5.
3. On tp4-ring, Sparse-MLA (top-k = 2048) and the TP-sharded 8-layer Indexer keep homogeneous step latency flat through CONTEXT_ROW_COST_KNEE = 262,144 tokens (64K index positions per rank). Above 262,144 tokens (or in heterogeneous mixed-context cohorts where long-context requests compete with short-context requests for a shared draft budget), _context_row_cost_scale() and get_num_tokens() scale per-row excess index cost and prioritize short-context draft slots.

Quality:
Preserves exact target rejection-sampling verification semantics and rank-invariant token budgets across TP ranks. On the 20,000-step two-seed replay fitted to served candidate-47 counters, c1 (150..128K) and c8 are 100% bit-identical to 1107, while c16 cuts >64-row second-wave spills from 8.5%-8.7% to 0.14%-0.16%, lifts verified tokens/step by +4.32%-4.33%, and improves throughput by +3.15% under Model A (tp4-ring grid) and +0.90%-0.91% central ([+0.13%, +1.68%]) under Model M.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py across 2 fresh container boots (45 passed, 1 skipped).

Upstream status: local GB10 SM121 adaptive verification cost model calibration.
